 Hypertension is a sustained elevation of arterial blood pressure. It is commonly defined as a systolic pressure at or above 140 mmHg or a diastolic pressure at or above 90 mmHg.
Anaemia is a reduction in the haemoglobin concentration or the red blood cell count, and it commonly results from iron deficiency.
